# Intent: The seeker's "always" watch looks when a sensor says something happened (a sound rise, a touch on the head, a bump) and otherwise only once every 30 s as a safety net (it was a frame a second, so the camera-on cue was lit about all the time). After a sighting it looks every 2 s for 20 s. Every look is two frames and still asks for the cue first; mute, lock, vision off, full quiet, night and the host lease still stop it, and a trigger seen while a gate is closed is dropped.
# Placement: unit
# Upstream: firmware/main/hal (ours)
# Check after a flash: self.look.status in always mode shows about two looks a minute in an empty room; a tap on the head causes one look within a second, with the cue lit before it; muted, locked or vision off: no look at all.
# Kconfig: none
# Memory cost: ms_t grows 12 bytes (in PSRAM with the seek state); the sound detector is 16 bytes of static; no task, no buffer.

